// A cross-service USE CASE, as a LikeC4 dynamic view. One journey per file, at
// FLEET level — `likec4.config.json` scopes the project to `architecture/`, so a
// view stored under `services/<svc>/` would resolve only that service's own
// containers and could never draw a journey across the fleet.
//
// The view states the INTERACTION and states no outcome. What must be true at
// each branch lives where outcomes are graded — an architecture requirement,
// joined to this view by `Covers: view:checkoutJourney` (see
// services/order-service/arch.spec.md). A diagram carrying its own expectations
// would be a second requirement corpus that can disagree with the first.
//
// `#smoke` is a GROUP: groups are tags rather than directories, because one
// journey belongs to several suites at once. The tag is declared once in the
// landscape's `specification` block — LikeC4 refuses an undeclared tag, so a
// mistyped group is a parse error rather than a silently-created second suite.
// `loam flow env smoke` answers which services must be up to run it, and
// `loam flow sync` regenerates architecture/flow-groups.likec4 from it.
views {
  dynamic view checkoutJourney {
    #smoke
    title 'Checkout: place an order and authorize its payment'
    description '''
      Every step below matches a relationship the landscape declares, which is
      what lets loam reach the operationId behind it — a parsed step carries no
      `metadata { op }` of its own, so the join is by (source, target).
    '''

    marketplace.checkoutWeb -> marketplace.orderService 'places the order'
    marketplace.orderService -> marketplace.identityService 'introspects the caller token'
    marketplace.orderService -> marketplace.paymentService 'authorizes the payment'
    alt {
      // Two branches, so this journey has TWO outcomes, and `flow.uncovered`
      // wants at least two covering scenarios. It never says WHICH outcome is
      // uncovered: loam does not read tests, so a shortfall is all it can prove.
      when 'authorized' {
        marketplace.paymentService -> kafka.paymentEvents 'PaymentAuthorized'
        kafka.paymentEvents -> marketplace.orderService 'advances the order once'
      }
      else {
        marketplace.orderService -> marketplace.paymentService 'refunds what was taken'
      }
    }
  }
}
